.TE
.PP
\f[B]Handled sequence types:\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]CSI\f[R] (Control Sequence Introducer): \f[CR]ESC [\f[R] parameters
final\-byte
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]8\-bit CSI\f[R]: Single byte 0x9B followed by parameters and
final\-byte
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]OSC\f[R] (Operating System Command): \f[CR]ESC ]\f[R] \&...
\f[CR]BEL\f[R] or \f[CR]ESC \(rs\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Two\-character escapes\f[R]: \f[CR]ESC\f[R] + final byte
(0x40\-0x7E)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Charset designators\f[R]: \f[CR]ESC (\f[R] or \f[CR]ESC )\f[R] +
one byte
.PP
The output is always less than or equal to the input in length, so
\f[B]in\-place operation is safe\f[R]: \f[CR]out\f[R] may alias
\f[CR]in\f[R].
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]st\f[R] \(em Pointer to the strip state.
Must be zero\-initialized before the first call (use \f[CR]memset\f[R]
or aggregate initialization).
The \f[CR]active\f[R] field must be set to 1 to enable stripping.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]in\f[R] \(em Input buffer containing raw bytes (may include ANSI
sequences).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]in_len\f[R] \(em Number of bytes in the input buffer.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]out\f[R] \(em Output buffer for clean (stripped) bytes.
May be the same pointer as \f[B]in\f[R] for in\-place operation.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]out_size\f[R] \(em Size of the output buffer in bytes.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of clean bytes written to \f[B]out\f[R].
This value is always in the range [0, min(in_len, out_size)].
.PP
Returns 0 if the entire input consisted of escape sequences.
